# oracle-roster.template — Oracle ID to Gitter Matrix ID mapping
#
# Copy this into your instance's config directory as oracle-roster.conf and
# fill in real handles. Used by oracle-network-status.sh v1.3+ for @ mention
# notifications.
#
# Format: ID|@matrix_handle:server[|Display Name]
#   - One entry per line
#   - Lines starting with # are comments
#   - Gitter users: @username:gitter.im
#   - Matrix users: @username:matrix.org
#   - Third field is optional (v1.8.2+), see below
#
# Display-name override (v1.8.2+):
# The optional third field replaces the operator name the daemon reports for
# that slot, both in the operator rows and in the HTML mention pill, so the
# name and the ping agree. Leave the field off, or empty, to keep whatever
# getoracles returns.
#
# You need this when the reported name is not the operator holding the slot.
# Those names come from a single slot-indexed list in the client that is not
# chain-aware, so a mainnet node can report testnet operator names wherever
# the two rosters assign a slot to different people.
#
# One roster per instance:
# Do NOT share one roster file between a mainnet and a testnet instance, and
# do not symlink them together. Slot assignments are per chain, so the same
# slot number can belong to different operators on each, and a shared file
# will ping the wrong one. Give each instance its own copy and set
# ROSTER_FILE in that instance's config, since the script's built-in default
# points at ~/.oracle-monitor/ regardless of which config was loaded.
#
# Dual-slot operators: if one person runs multiple oracles (e.g. slots 0+28),
# list the SAME handle for both. The script deduplicates — they'll only get
# one ping per run regardless of how many of their oracles are down.
#
# Where to find handles:
#   - Gitter People list (sidebar) shows @handle:gitter.im
#   - Matrix room member list via Element
#   - Gitter JSON export: grep "sender" export.json | sort -u
#
# Example:
# 0|@jared:gitter.im
# 4|@shenger:gitter.im
# 11|@someoperator:gitter.im|Some Operator
# 17|@digibyte-maxi:gitter.im
